---
import PageContainer from "../components/layout/PageContainer.astro";
import ContentSection from "../components/ui/ContentSection.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="About"
    heading="A brief autobiography"
    description="How mathematics, computer science, research, and computer systems fit together for me."
>
    <PageContainer class="space-y-6">
        <ContentSection id="background" title="Background">
            <p>
                I’m a Computer Science and Mathematics Joint Honours Co-op
                student at the University of Manitoba, with a minor in
                Statistics. I was born and raised in Winnipeg, and my choice of
                degree has always been driven by passion: I enjoy the rigour of
                mathematics and the process of turning an idea into a working
                program.
            </p>
            <p>
                My interest in computing began with programming in high school
                and grew into a broader curiosity about how computers work—from
                the logic of algorithms to the design of operating systems.
            </p>
        </ContentSection>

        <ContentSection id="interests" title="Technical interests">
            <p>
                My main academic interests include discrete algorithms,
                computational geometry, and scientific computing. On the systems
                side, I’m interested in low-level, operating-system, and
                embedded programming.
            </p>
            <p>
                I enjoy moving between theory and implementation: analyzing an
                algorithm on paper, proving why it works, and then building a
                clear, efficient implementation. I have worked with Java,
                Python, C/C#/C++, JavaScript, and Julia. My IDE of choice is
                Neovim.
            </p>
        </ContentSection>

        <ContentSection
            id="research-and-teaching"
            title="Research and teaching"
        >
            <p>
                In Summer 2025, I researched a problem in computational geometry
                and discrete optimization with Dr. Stéphane Durocher at the
                University of Manitoba. I also enjoy teaching mathematics,
                whether in tutorials, the Math Help Centre, or an informal
                conversation about an interesting problem.
            </p>
        </ContentSection>

        <ContentSection id="outside-work" title="Outside the work">
            <p>
                Away from coursework and projects, I like reading (mostly
                textbooks), going to the gym, refining my Linux environment, and
                spending time with friends. This site is where I collect the
                work I’m proud of and document what I learn next.
            </p>
        </ContentSection>
    </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>
